msgid ""
"More fields may be added to this struct at any time, so its exact layout "
"and size should not be relied upon."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/threading.rst:79
msgid "returns a UV_E* error code on failure"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/threading.rst:83
msgid ""
"Detaches a thread. Detached threads automatically release their resources"
" upon termination, eliminating the need for the application to call "
"`uv_thread_join`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/threading.rst:91
msgid ""
"Like :c:func:`uv_thread_create`, but additionally specifies options for "
"creating a new thread."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/threading.rst:93
msgid ""
"If `UV_THREAD_HAS_STACK_SIZE` is set, `stack_size` specifies a stack size"
" for the new thread. `0` indicates that the default value should be used,"
" i.e. behaves as if the flag was not set. Other values will be rounded up"
" to the nearest page boundary."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/threading.rst:101
msgid ""
"Sets the specified thread's affinity to cpumask, which is specified in "
"bytes. Optionally returning the previous affinity setting in oldmask. On "
"Unix, uses :man:`pthread_getaffinity_np(3)` to get the affinity setting "
"and maps the cpu_set_t to bytes in oldmask. Then maps the bytes in "
"cpumask to a cpu_set_t and uses :man:`pthread_setaffinity_np(3)`. On "
"Windows, maps the bytes in cpumask to a bitmask and uses "
"SetThreadAffinityMask() which returns the previous affinity setting."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/threading.rst:109
msgid ""
"The mask_size specifies the number of entries (bytes) in cpumask / "
"oldmask, and must be greater-than-or-equal-to :c:func:`uv_cpumask_size`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/threading.rst:113
msgid "Thread affinity setting is not atomic on Windows. Unsupported on macOS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/threading.rst:119
msgid ""
"Gets the specified thread's affinity setting. On Unix, this maps the "
"cpu_set_t returned by :man:`pthread_getaffinity_np(3)` to bytes in "
"cpumask."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/threading.rst:122
msgid ""
"The mask_size specifies the number of entries (bytes) in cpumask, and "
"must be greater-than-or-equal-to :c:func:`uv_cpumask_size`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/threading.rst:126
msgid "Thread affinity getting is not atomic on Windows. Unsupported on macOS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/threading.rst:132
msgid "Gets the CPU number on which the calling thread is running."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/threading.rst:135
msgid "Currently only implemented on Windows, Linux and FreeBSD."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/threading.rst:145
msgid ""
"Sets the name of the current thread. Different platforms define different"
" limits on the max number of characters a thread name can be: Linux, IBM "
"i (16), macOS (64), Windows (32767), and NetBSD (32), etc. "
"`uv_thread_setname()` will truncate it in case `name` is larger than the "
"limit of the platform."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/threading.rst:149 ../../src/threading.rst:162
msgid "Not supported on Windows Server 2016, returns `UV_ENOSYS`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/threading.rst:155
msgid ""
"Gets the name of the thread specified by `tid`. The thread name is "
"copied, with the trailing NUL, into the buffer pointed to by `name`. The "
"`size` parameter specifies the size of the buffer pointed to by `name`. "
"The buffer should be large enough to hold the name of the thread plus the"
" trailing NUL, or it will be truncated to fit with the trailing NUL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/threading.rst:160 ../../src/threading.rst:176
#: ../../src/threading.rst:188
msgid "It's undefined behavior to call this after the thread has terminated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/threading.rst:168
msgid ""
"If the function succeeds, the return value is 0. If the function fails, "
"the return value is less than zero. Sets the scheduling priority of the "
"thread specified by tid. It requires elevated privilege to set specific "
"priorities on some platforms. The priority can be set to the following "
"constants. UV_THREAD_PRIORITY_HIGHEST, UV_THREAD_PRIORITY_ABOVE_NORMAL, "
"UV_THREAD_PRIORITY_NORMAL, UV_THREAD_PRIORITY_BELOW_NORMAL, "
"UV_THREAD_PRIORITY_LOWEST."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/threading.rst:182
msgid ""
"If the function succeeds, the return value is 0. If the function fails, "
"the return value is less than zero. Retrieves the scheduling priority of "
"the thread specified by tid. The value in the output parameter priority "
"is platform dependent. For Linux, when schedule policy is SCHED_OTHER "
"(default), priority is 0."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/threading.rst:193
msgid "Thread-local storage"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/threading.rst:196
msgid ""
"The total thread-local storage size may be limited. That is, it may not "
"be possible to create many TLS keys."
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/threading.rst:205
msgid "Once-only initialization"
msgstr ""

#: ../../src/threading.rst:207
msgid ""
"Runs a function once and only once. Concurrent calls to :c:func:`uv_once`"
" with the same guard will block all callers except one (it's unspecified "
"which one). The guard should be initialized statically with the "
"UV_ONCE_INIT macro."
msgstr ""

